    route: "/components", page: "Components", section: "", text: "components follow shadcn/ui's composition style: a component's text and\nparts are its children, not props.\n\n text goes in children\n\ntext children fill a component's label. a text with a variant styles part\nof it.  compose parts\n\nlarger components are built from named parts, such as dialogtrigger and\ndialogcontent, or tableheader and tablerow. each part takes its own\nclassname.  your own components\n\nwrite a props interface and a function. children?: child[] accepts nested\ncontent, which you pass on to a container.  icons\n\nicon props and <icon name=\"...\" /> take any of the 1,830 lucide icon name", keywords: "guide docs components"
  }, {
    route: "/components", page: "Components", section: "Text goes in children", text: "", keywords: "guide docs"
  }, {
    route: "/state-and-reactivity", page: "State and Reactivity", section: "", text: "state lives in signals. reading signal.get() inside tsrx markup makes that part of\nthe tree update when the signal changes; nothing else re-renders.\n\n signals computed(() => ...) names a derived value; it re-evaluates when read.\n\n controlled and uncontrolled\n\na form control is controlled when you pass its value (checked, value,\nselected, open) and update it from the change event. leave the value out\nand the control keeps its own state; defaultchecked, defaultvalue or\ndefaultopen set where it starts.  conditional content\n\na ternary that reads a signal swaps subtrees; hidden keeps a subtree but\n", keywords: "guide docs state and reactivity"
  }, {
